{"description":"Fix project-scoped execution state display in `eka status` and resolve project-scoped `ses:execution-state` retrieval","acceptanceCriteria":"- `eka status` execution section shows the execution state of the current project/repo only.\n- `eka get ses:execution-state` resolves against current project and returns the correct execution state.\n- If the current project has no execution-state record, result is project-scoped not-found.\n- Qualified form `ekax namespace/ses:execution-state` remains unchanged.\n- Tests with two projects and distinct execution state records validate per-project isolation.","impact":"Prevents agents and operators from seeing the wrong execution state, which could lead to execution of the wrong project."}